Golden seed-data fixtures for internal/seed tests.

nine-section.golden.tar is generated by the vendored verbatim writeSeed
copy in seed_test.go (incus-osd/cmd/image-customizer writeSeed) under
incus-osd pin v0.0.0-20260815030500-0f5b8057f2fc and
go.yaml.in/yaml/v4 v4.0.0-rc.6 (matching upstream go.mod).
kernel.golden.yaml and security.golden.yaml are Render output for the
CLI-exclusive sections writeSeed does not emit; they use the same
yaml.Dump(..., yaml.WithV2Defaults()) call.

A pin bump of incus-osd or yaml/v4 that changes dump or tar layout
explains golden churn.

Residual gap: these bytes are not compared against an upstream-built
customizer binary. The oracle is the vendored writeSeed source under the
same yaml/v4 pin, not a binary built from upstream.
